    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f325783e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of young men with their faces obscured, raising their hands in a gesture that could be interpreted as celebratory or defiant. The overlaid text reads, 'if this is what they call pride.. then i don't wanna see what they call shame.' This juxtaposition implies a negative judgment of the group's behavior, suggesting that their display of pride is so extreme or inappropriate that it makes the concept of shame seem even more undesirable. The meme uses a sarcastic and dismissive tone to convey contempt for the group's actions or identity, which can be seen as a direct attack based on their appearance or behavior. While the specific target group is not explicitly identified, the visual and textual elements together create a hostile and derogatory message, fitting the definition of a hateful meme as it attacks or devalues a group based on their presentation or actions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1891af7e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
