      "instance_name": "stereotype_of_young_men_as_uneducated_or_unskilled",
      "label": "Stereotype: Young men as uneducated or lacking in social skills",
      "description": "The meme's tone suggests contempt for the group's perceived lack of sophistication or social awareness. This stereotype is often used to dismiss or belittle groups perceived as 'simple' or 'unrefined'. The phrase 'then i don't wanna see what they call shame' implies that the group's 'pride' is so crude or embarrassing that their 'shame' would be even more so — a rhetorical device that relies on the stereotype that young men (or certain groups) are not capable of nuanced behavior or social decorum.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
